# Socket stack

Read `docs/wiki/Socket-Stack.md`. Spec: `docs/wiki/Coding-Standards.md` §8.

- `ConnectionHandler` = wire only (Noise, framing, IQ, keep-alive). Features register on `NodeDispatcher`.
- One IQ/operation per `UseCase`. Header: purpose, what it does not do, `Ports: rc14 <path>`.
- Host seams in `Abstractions/`. Do not take WinRT or Core ViewModels in Socket.
- Attach message/media/app-state/groups from the host (`SocketBridge`), not by bloating `WhatsAppSession` with domain state.
- LID mapping is `LidMappingStore`, not a new JidAlias table.
- `TransferSocketToBrokerAsync` / reclaim stay false until the session can lend the transport.

Do not compile `SocketClient.cs`. Do not add protocol switches back onto `WhatsAppService`.
